{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"733827637901787206","content":"Web sighs deeply. They think of leaving London, and how they still aren't sure it was the right choice. They think of joining the Golden Dawn. They think of burning down Jennerus Jack's shop. They think of lying to their friends, not leaving the Golden Dawn sooner. They think of sentencing Rah to death, then being too ashamed to even remember it. They remember choosing to look away as the Golden Dawn hurt Amara, letting her be controlled. They think of ruining her choices, how maybe they could have let her live. They think of forgetting Skitter, their own brother. They think of not telling Baeshra that the sub might be destroyed, causing her to lose so many of her possessions. They think of not telling Baeshra about the stone sooner. They think of ruining the colony's talk with the fishmother, and how they hurt Sandigill. They think of not pushing harder at the hag impersonating Wren, how maybe they could have saved the others sooner. They think of being careless the first time they raised the dead, corrupting the ground and making Wynne re-live being captured by hags. They think of how the hags returning to the ground made their curse last much longer. They think of dividing the town about necromancy, instead of bringing them together. They think of how they abandoned the puckwudgies for a time. They think of how still now, empty hill is ruling over them.","created_at":"2020-08-20T03:30:42.136000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"745847252366393346","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
